oint summary/session metadata through checkpoint stores\n- show checkpoint ID, agent, and summary/fallback text\n- enrich static output and selected-line TUI header\n- degrade per-commit when metadata is missing or malformed\n\nTests: plain commit, commit with trailer and metadata, trailer with missing checkpoint, multi-session checkpoint overview fields.\n\n**PR 3: Detail Navigation Without Session Drilldown**\n\nAdd `enter`/space drilldown from a selected blame block:\n\n- checkpoint detail when `Entire-Checkpoint` exists\n- generic Git commit fallback otherwise\n- file-scoped diff for the selected path\n- `esc`/`q` back behavior\n- checkpoint detail shows ID, commit, agent, summary/fallback, files, session count, tokens when present\n\nTests: key transitions, checkpoint detail rendering, Git fallback rendering, file-scoped diff command behavior.\n\n**PR 4: Checkpoint Detail Pane Model**\n\nReplace the simple detail screen with the spec’s pane structure:\n\n- `Sessions`\n- `Generated Checkpoint Summary`\n- `File Diff`\n- `tab` focus cycling\n- focused pane gets expanded rendering and scroll ownership\n- unfocused panes render previews\n\nTests: pane focus, preview/expanded rendering, scroll ownership, `g`/`G`.\n\n**PR 5: Session Detail Drilldown**\n\nAdd explicit session selection and session detail:\n\n- session list supports movement and open\n- session detail reuses/mirrors `entire explain --checkpoint` condensed transcript rendering\n- initially keep it scrollable and readable before adding the more complex tool-call focus behavior\n\nTests: multi-session navigation, session content loading by index/ID, transcript fallback behavior.\n\n**PR 6: Session Interaction Polish**\n\nAdd the richer session transcript behavior:\n\n- tool-call-heavy stretches collapsed by default\n- tool-call groups as bordered sections\n- `tab` / `shift+tab` moves between tool-call groups\n- `e` expands/collapses focused group\n- viewport keeps focused group visible\n\nTests: group extraction/rendering, focus movement, expand/collapse, viewport positioning.\n\n**PR 7: Highlighting And Diff Polish**\n\nAdd Chroma-backed rendering:\n\n- syntax-highlight only the TUI code pane\n- preserve metadata gutter styling through Lip Gloss\n- improve diff rendering with add/remove colors and hunk preservation\n- fallback cleanly when lexer detection fails\n\nNote: Chroma is currently indirect in `go.mod`; importing it directly will make it a direct dependency, so I would treat this PR as the explicit dependency/polish PR.\n\n**PR 8: No-Arg File Browser**\n\nAdd `entire why` interactive entry:\n\n- browser rooted at current working directory, not repo root\n- dotfiles included\n- directories before files\n- traversal via arrows, `j/k`, `enter`, `h`, backspace\n- preserve browser directory/cursor when returning from file view\n- non-interactive no-arg and forced `--interactive` without TTY fail clearly\n\nTests: sort order, path normalization to repo-relative Git path, state preservation, non-interactive failure.\n\nI’d keep the command hidden through the whole prototype series, then do a tiny final “unhide or keep hidden” PR when the feature is ready for broader use.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
