nless explicitly requested.\n- Do not create commits unless the user explicitly asks.\n\n---\n\n## PR 1: Hidden Enriched Overview With Highlighting\n\n### Task 1: Add The Hidden Cobra Command Shell\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/why.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/root.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/why_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/root_test.go`\n\n**Step 1: Write command registration tests**\n\nAdd tests that assert:\n\n- `entire why` exists.\n- `why` is hidden.\n- `why` accepts `-L`, `--lines`, `-i` / `--interactive`, and `--no-pager`.\n- no positional path in non-interactive mode returns an error.\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestWhy|TestRoot' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: fail because `newWhyCmd` does not exist.\n\n**Step 2: Add the command shell**\n\nCreate `newWhyCmd()` in `why.go` with:\n\n- `Use: \"why [path]\"`\n- `Hidden: true`\n- `Args: cobra.MaximumNArgs(1)`\n- flags for `-L`, `--lines`, `-i`, `--interactive`, and `--no-pager`\n- `RunE` that delegates to `runWhy(ctx, out, errOut, options)`\n\nRegister it in `NewRootCmd()` near `newExplainCmd()`.\n\n**Step 3: Run the command registration tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestWhy|TestRoot' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: pass for command registration; later behavior tests may still be pending.\n\n### Task 2: Add Option Parsing And Path Validation\n\n**Files:**\n- Create/modify: `cmd/entire/cli/why.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/why_test.go`\n\n**Step 1: Write tests for line ranges**\n\nCover:\n\n- empty input means no range\n- `7` becomes git range `7,7`\n- `3-8` becomes git range `3,8`\n- `0`, `8-3`, `a-b`, and `3:` fail\n- `-L` and `--lines` accept identical forms\n\n**Step 2: Write tests for target path normalization**\n\nUse `testutil.InitRepo`, `testutil.WriteFile`, `testutil.GitAdd`, `testutil.GitCommit`, and `t.Chdir(repoDir)` only in tests that do not call `t.Parallel()`.\n\nCover:\n\n- relative path from repo root resolves to git path\n- absolute path inside repo resolves to git path\n- path outside repo is rejected\n- path missing at `HEAD` is rejected even if present only in working tree\n\n**Step 3: Implement parsing and validation**\n\nAdd small helpers:\n\n- `parseWhyLineRange(raw string) (whyLineRange, error)`\n- `resolveWhyPath(ctx context.Context, input string) (repoRoot string, gitPath string, absPath string, err error)`\n- `whyPathExistsAtHEAD(ctx context.Context, repoRoot, gitPath string) error`\n\nUse `git cat-file -e HEAD:<path>` or go-git tree lookup. If using git CLI, run it with `cmd.Dir = repoRoot`.\n\n**Step 4: Run focused tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestWhyLineRange|TestWhyPath' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: pass.\n\n### Task 3: Parse `git blame --line-porcelain`\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/why_blame.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/why_blame_test.go`\n\n**Step 1: Write parser fixture tests**\n\nUse inline porcelain fixtures covering:\n\n- one block with multiple lines\n- repeated metadata elision in porcelain output\n- author name and author-time\n- filename with spaces\n- line contents beginning with tab after the porcelain content marker\n\nAssert parsed records include:\n\n- full commit hash\n- original line number\n- final file line number\n- author\n- author time\n- source text\n\n**Step 2: Implement blame invocation**\n\nAdd:\n\n- `runGitBlame(ctx, repoRoot, gitPath string, lineRange *whyLineRange) ([]byte, error)`\n- `parseBlamePorcelain(data []byte) ([]whyBlameLine, error)`\n\nInvoke:\n\n```text\ngit blame --line-porcelain [-L start,end] -- <gitPath>\n```\n\nSet `cmd.Dir = repoRoot`. Capture stderr and include it in errors.\n\n**Step 3: Collapse contiguous blame blocks**\n\nAdd:\n\n- `collapseWhyBlameBlocks(lines []whyBlameLine) []whyBlameBlock`\n- row model that stores `BlockIndex` for each line\n\nContiguous means adjacent rendered rows have the same commit hash.\n\n**Step 4: Run parser tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestParseBlame|TestCollapseWhyBlame' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: pass.\n\n### Task 4: Add Local Entire Metadata Enrichment\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/why_enrich.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/why_enrich_test.go`\n\n**Step 1: Write unit tests around commit enrichment**\n\nUse temp repos and go-git where possible. Cover:\n\n- commit without `Entire-Checkpoint` returns plain Git metadata\n- commit with valid trailer but missing checkpoint degrades without aborting\n- commit with local checkpoint reads checkpoint ID, agent, session count, files touched, and summary/fallback\n- corrupted checkpoint metadata degrades for that commit only\n\n**Step 2: Implement local lookup**\n\nAdd:\n\n- `newWhyCheckpointLookup(ctx, repo) (*whyCheckpointLookup, error)`\n- `enrichWhyCommits(ctx, repo, lookup, blocks) map[plumbing.Hash]whyCommitInfo`\n- `readWhyCheckpointInfo(ctx, lookup, cpID) (whyCheckpointInfo, error)`\n\nThe lookup should mirror the useful parts of `newExplainCheckpointLookup`, but it must not fetch remotes.\n\nUse:\n\n- `checkpoint.NewGitStore(repo)`\n- `checkpoint.NewV2GitStore(repo, v2URL)`\n- `settings.IsCheckpointsV2Enabled(ctx)`\n- `checkpoint.ResolveCommittedReaderForCheckpoint(...)`\n- `readLatestSessionContentForExplain(...)` or a small local equivalent if exporting an explain helper is not appropriate\n\n**Step 3: Implement fallback summary policy**\n\nSummary precedence:\n\n1. generated summary intent/outcome from session metadata\n2. first prompt line from checkpoint content\n3. commit subject\n4. `(not generated)`\n\nUse existing `strategy.TruncateDescription` for compact display.\n\n**Step 4: Run enrichment tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestWhyEnrich' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: pass.\n\n### Task 5: Add Static Renderer And Mode Selection\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/why.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/why_render.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/why_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/why_render_test.go`\n\n**Step 1: Write renderer tests**\n\nAssert static output includes:\n\n- line number\n- short commit hash\n- author\n- checkpoint ID when present\n- agent when present\n- source line\n- fallback values for non-Entire commits\n\nAlso assert `--lines` restricts displayed rows.\n\n**Step 2: Implement mode selection**\n\nTUI path requires all of:\n\n- not `ACCESSIBLE=1`\n- output writer is terminal-capable\n- `interactive.CanPromptInteractively()`\n\nStatic path is used for:\n\n- piped stdout\n- accessibility mode\n- `--no-pager`\n- any non-interactive environment\n\nIf `--interactive` is set and the TUI requirements are not met, return a clear error.\n\n**Step 3: Implement static output**\n\nUse a blame-like gutter, for example:\n\n```text\nLINE COMMIT  AUTHOR           CHECKPOINT    AGENT          CODE\n  12 a1b2c3d  Pat Example      fc03fc03fc03 claude-code    func main() {\n```\n\nKeep columns stable and truncate long author/agent fields with existing string helpers.\n\n**Step 4: Reuse pager behavior**\n\nUse `outputExplainContent(w, content, noPager)` for static output.\n\n**Step 5: Run focused tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestWhy.*Static|TestWhy.*Mode|TestRenderWhy' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: pass.\n\n### Task 6: Add Chroma Source Highlighting For TUI Rows\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `go.mod`\n- Modify: `go.sum`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/why_highlight.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/why_highlight_test.go`\n\n**Step 1: Confirm dependency approval**\n\nChroma is currently an indirect dependency in `go.mod`. Importing it from `why_highlight.go` will make it a direct dependency. Stop and confirm with the user before implementing this task if approval has not already been given for adding Chroma as a direct dependency.\n\n**Step 2: Write highlighting tests**\n\nCover:\n\n- known extension selects a lexer\n- unknown extension returns plain code\n- highlighting returns one rendered string per input source line\n- empty files and trailing newline do not