e model from the start.\n- PR 3: session detail drilldown with condensed transcript rendering.\n- PR 4: rich session transcript controls for collapsible tool-call groups.\n- PR 5: no-arg interactive file browser.\n- PR 6: release polish and unhide decision.\n\nDo not implement remote checkpoint fetching, arbitrary revisions, JSON output, rename/copy tracking, automatic summary generation, or uncommitted working-tree attribution.\n\n## Existing Code To Reuse\n\n- Command registration: `cmd/entire/cli/root.go`\n- Explain checkpoint lookup helpers and formatting references: `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go`\n- Pager helper: `outputExplainContent` / `outputWithPager` in `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go`\n- Bubble Tea navigation/rendering patterns: `cmd/entire/cli/search_tui.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/activity_tui.go`\n- Terminal/accessibility gating: `cmd/entire/cli/interactive/interactive.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/utils.go`\n- Shared terminal styles: `cmd/entire/cli/status_style.go`\n- Checkpoint readers and metadata types: `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/checkpoint.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed_reader_resolve.go`\n- Trailer parsing: `cmd/entire/cli/trailers/trailers.go`\n- Repo-root path handling: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/paths.go`\n- Git diff-tree helper style: `cmd/entire/cli/gitops/diff.go`\n- Test repo helpers: `cmd/entire/cli/testutil/testutil.go`\n- Integration test environment, if needed: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/testenv.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/hooks.go`\n\n## Implementation Rules\n\n- Keep `entire why` hidden until PR 6 decides otherwise.\n- Use local-only metadata resolution. Do not call `FetchMetadataTreeOnly`, `FetchMetadataFromCheckpointRemote`, `FetchV2MainTreeOnly`, or any remote fallback from the why command.\n- Use repo root for git-relative paths. Do not build git paths from `os.Getwd()` except for the file browser root itself.\n- Preserve static output for non-interactive environments and `ACCESSIBLE=1`.\n- `--interactive` must fail clearly when a