kpoint once.\n   - Apply the same checkpoint info to every commit that references it.\n\n4. Avoid repeated root lookups:\n   - For all target checkpoint IDs, resolve the v1/v2 root tree once, then read the needed checkpoint subtrees from that root.\n   - I would not start with `ListCommitted()` unless target IDs are numerous; it scans all checkpoints, while we only need the IDs present in the blamed file.\n\nLarger later options: lazy-load Entire metadata after the first TUI render, cache checkpoint overview data in memory across navigation, or persist a small checkpoint overview index. I’d start with steps 1-3; that should move this from seconds toward the `git blame` baseline without changing the user-visible behavior much.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
