he final pane model from the start.\n- PR 3: session detail drilldown with condensed transcript rendering.\n- PR 4: rich session transcript controls for collapsible tool-call groups.\n- PR 5: no-arg interactive file browser.\n- PR 6: release polish and unhide decision.\n\nDo not implement remote checkpoint fetching, arbitrary revisions, JSON output, line-range flags such as `-L` / `--lines`, rename/copy tracking, automatic summary generation, or uncommitted working-tree attribution.\n\nLine-range focused entry is intentionally deferred. It needs a later design pass because a partial-file invocation does not fit cleanly with the first iteration's full-file TUI browsing model.\n\n## Existing Code To Reuse\n\n- Command registration: `cmd/entire/cli/root.go`\n- Explain checkpoint lookup helpers and formatting references: `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go`\n- Pager helper: `outputExplainContent` / `outputWithPager` in `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go`\n- Bubble Tea navigation/rendering patterns: `cmd/entire/cli/search_tui.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/activity_tui.go`\n- Shared TUI key bindings: `cmd/entire/cli/keys.go`\n- Terminal/accessibility gating: `cmd/entire/cli/interactive/interactive.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/utils.go`\n- Shared terminal styles: `cmd/entire/cli/status_style.go`\n- Checkpoint readers and metadata types: `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/checkpoint.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed_reader_resolve.go`\n- Trailer parsing: `cmd/entire/cli/trailers/trailers.go`\n- Repo-root path handling: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/paths.go`\n- Git diff-tree helper style: `cmd/entire/cli/gitops/diff.go`\n- Test repo helpers: `cmd/entire/cli/testutil/testutil.go`\n- Integration test environment, if needed: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/testenv.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/hooks.go`\n\n## Implementation Rules\n\n- Keep `entire why` hidden until PR 6 decides otherwise.\n- Use local-only metadata resolution. Do not call `FetchMetadataTreeOnly`, `FetchMetadataFromCheckpointRemote`, `FetchV2MainTreeOnly`, or any remote fallback from the why command.\n- Use repo root for git-relative paths. Do not build git paths from `os.Getwd()` except for the file browser root itself.\n- Preserve static output for non-interactive environments and `ACCESSIBLE=1`.\n- Mode selection is automatic: use the TUI only when accessibility is off, stdout is terminal-capable, and interactive prompting is possible; otherwise use static output.\n- All why TUIs must use the shared `keys` bindings from `cmd/entire/cli/keys.go` for common controls instead of new ad hoc key strings.\n- Common TUI semantics are: `enter` selects/opens, `esc` backs out of nested modes or cancels, `q` / `ctrl+c` quits, arrows plus `j` / `k` move or scroll, and `home` / `end` plus `g` / `G` jump to top/bottom.\n- Footer help should follow the current activity/search TUI style: width-aware, no overflow, full aliases on wide layouts such as `↑/↓, j/k scroll` and `home/end, g/G top/bottom`, and reduced primary controls on narrow layouts.\n- After editing Go files, run `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, and `golangci-lint run ./...`.\n- Do not run real E2E tests unless explicitly requested.\n- Do not create commits unless the user explicitly asks.\n\n---\n\n## PR 1: Hidden Enriched Overview With Highlighting\n\n### Task 1: Add The Hidden Cobra Command Shell\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/why.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/root.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/why_test.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/root_test.go`\n\n**Step 1: Write command registration tests**\n\nAdd tests that assert:\n\n- `entire why` exists.\n- `why` is hidden.\n- `why` does not register `-i` / `--interactive` or `…2566 chars truncated…\ngit blame --line-porcelain -- <gitPath>\n```\n\nSet `cmd.Dir = repoRoot`. Capture stderr and include it in errors.\n\nIf blame fails because the path is missing, is a directory, or is otherwise not blameable at `HEAD`, return a clear error based on the `git blame` failure. Do not add a separate preflight existence check.\n\n**Step 3: Collapse contiguous blame blocks**\n\nAdd:\n\n- `collapseWhyBlameBlocks(lines []whyBlameLine) []whyBlameBlock`\n- row model that stores `BlockIndex` for each line\n\nContiguous means adjacent rendered rows have the same commit hash.\n\n**Step 4: Run parser tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'TestParseBlame|TestCollapseWhyBlame' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: pass.\n\n### Task 4: Add Local Entire Metadata Enrichment\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/why_enrich.go`\n- Test: `cmd/entire/cli/why_enrich_test.go`\n\n**Step 1: Write unit tests around commit enrichment**\n\nUse temp repos and go-git where possible. Cover:\n\n- commit without `Entire-Checkpoint` returns plain Git metadata\n- commit with valid trailer but missing checkpoint degrades without aborting\n- commit with local checkpoint reads checkpoint ID, agent, session count, files touched, and summary/fallback\n- corrupted checkpoint metadata degrades for that commit only\n\n**Step 2: Implement local lookup**\n\nAdd:\n\n- `newWhyCheckpointLookup(ctx, repo) (*whyCheckpointLookup, error)`\n- `enrichWhyCommits(ctx, repo, lookup, blocks) map[plumbing.Hash]whyCommitInfo`\n- `readWhyCheckpointInfo(ctx, lookup, cpID) (whyCheckpointInfo, error)`\n\nThe lookup should mirror the useful parts of `newExplainCheckpointLookup`, but it must not fetch remotes.\n\nUse:\n\n- `checkpoint.NewGitStore(repo)`\n- `checkpoint.NewV2GitStore(repo, v2URL)`\n- `settings.IsCheckpointsV2Enabled(ctx)`\n- `checkpoint.ResolveCommittedReaderForCheckpoint(...)`\n- `readLatestSessionContentForExplain(...)` or a small local equivalent if exporting an explain helper is not appropriate\n\n**Step 3: Implement fallback summary policy**\n\nSummary precedence:\n\n1. generated summary intent/outcome from session metadata\n2. first prompt line from checkpoint content\n3. commit subject\n4. `(not generated)`\n\nUse existing `strategy.TruncateDescription` for compact display.\n\n**Step 4: Run enrichment